<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Field map of the npc entity: which attribute of the client's npc table corresponds to which attribute of the
     server's npc file. It names files, elements and attributes only; it holds no row of either side.

     Made the same way as item.fieldmap.xml (see its header for the columns): the same ids were read on both sides
     of one shipped data set and every pair of fields was compared id by id; only ids with exactly one row and one
     <environment> on each side were compared ("sample"). A pair with different names is kept only when the values
     agree and at least 5 distinct values agree. loader = yes means the attribute name was also found in the
     client's npc loader (name evidence only: the loader is not proof of what the field does).

     The client keeps 1 file per 100000 ids (npcdata/NNN.xml, one <npc> row per id, read lazily per file); there is
     no index table, so a new id only needs a row in its file. The server keeps one file per id.
     Fields are written as element-path@attribute, the path counted from <environment>; "@level" is an attribute of
     <environment> itself on the client.

     Notes
       stat@hp, stat@pap, stat@map  low: the two sides differ on about 16% of the ids. Still kept equal by a mod,
                                    since the client shows the value and the server uses it.
       aiInfo@*, combat@*           present in the client table, but the client loader does not read them.
       effectdummy                  client only: the server file keeps it outside <environment>, if at all. -->
